== SOURCE
l:C_ := { x_ y z -> z x_ y }
== TITLE
C, the Cardinal: swapping arguments
== NOTE x_
A function
The function whose two arguments C swaps.
== NOTE y z
Two values
Named in the order C is given them.
== NOTE z x_ y
x z y
Written between two values, a function takes the left one, then the right one: `z x_ y` is x applied to z and then y. So the arguments come swapped: Dyalog `f⍨`, J `f~`, BQN `F˜` (with two arguments). The Warbler W, `{ x_ y -> y x_ y }`, gives one value to both sides: `f⍨` with one argument.
